This game is ancient, but for those looking to dust off some of the old LucasArts games:
- this is an odd expansion, viz b/c of random plot and unexplained inconsistencies with original game;
- it is incredibly short in length;
- the graphics, control and quality are inferior to the original, which doesn't make any sense.

The good:
-Original/Unique;
-Characters;
-Gameplay;
-Field of View of 90° (Modified via "fov_desired #");
-Fitting Soundtrack;
-Rebindable Keys.
-Supports Subtitles.
-Achievements;
-Trading Cards;
-Steam Cloud;
The bad:
-Short 18 Chapters (Around 5-6 hours);
-Voice Acting;
-Character Animations;
-Linear;
-Repetitive;
Score: 7/10.

